---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Governance decisions | Macro Evidence"
  description="The Macro Evidence Governance decision series: organization-level decisions that apply across repositories or to the organization's structure."
>
  <PageIntro
    kicker="Governance"
    title="Governance decisions"
    lead="Decisions that apply across Macro Evidence repositories or to its organizational structure."
  />

  <section class="section policy-page">
    <div class="site-container reading policy-reading-wide">
      <article class="policy-text">
        <p>
          This page lists Macro Evidence decisions that apply across multiple
          repositories or to the organization's structure. Repository-specific
          decisions stay in that repository's own&#32;<code>decisions/</code
          >&#32;directory. The shared ADR contract is defined in&#32;<a
            href="/governance/documentation-standards#5-architecture-decision-records"
            >Documentation Standards, section 5</a
          >.
        </p>
        <h2 id="decisions">Decisions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0001-evidence-paced-roadmap-and-shared-foundation-growth"
              >0001. Evidence-paced roadmap and shared-foundation product growth</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0002-license-governance-content-under-cc-by-sa-4-0"
              >0002. License governance content under CC BY-SA 4.0</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0003-license-github-community-infrastructure-under-cc-by-sa-4-0"
              >0003. License .github community infrastructure under CC BY-SA 4.0</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0004-adopt-tailored-contributor-covenant-3-0"
              >0004. Adopt tailored Contributor Covenant 3.0</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0005-establish-organization-wide-contribution-governance"
              >0005. Establish organization-wide contribution governance</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0006-preserve-licensing-flexibility-through-contributor-agreements"
              >0006. Preserve licensing flexibility through contributor
              agreements</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0007-keep-content-signals-intentionally-unspecified"
              >0007. Keep Content Signals intentionally unspecified</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0008-establish-mdd-as-an-organization-level-sibling-reference-layer"
              >0008. Establish MDD as an organization-level sibling reference
              layer</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0009-adopt-a-harmony-based-contributor-rights-system"
              >0009. Adopt a Harmony-based contributor-rights system</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0010-preserve-cc-by-sa-default-with-explicit-legal-form-exceptions"
              >0010. Preserve the governance CC BY-SA default with explicit
              legal-form exceptions</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0011-use-mixed-licensing-for-github-community-content-and-executable-automation"
              >0011. Use mixed licensing for .github community content and
              executable automation</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0012-define-github-contributor-rights-enforcement-architecture"
              >0012. Define GitHub contributor-rights enforcement architecture</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="/governance/decisions/0013-consolidate-governance-publication-into-the-website-repository"
              >0013. Consolidate governance publication into the website
              repository</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
